{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"636012145204527127","content":"Sir Percival’s religion is a religion of cunning. The Gunter Grifters are tolerated because they are registered with the government and are conscripted into every conflict. In this way, the thieves guild has flourished in England. Petty theft is largely ignored by the police, in return the thieves of England can pour into an enemy country unseen to undo a kingdom with never a single soldier unsheathing a blade.\n\nThe modern opinion of the followers of Sir Percival in Gunters Grifters is widely romanticized. There are few modern tales that don’t portray the members of the GG as swashbuckling heroes or misunderstood anti heroes, and thieves with hearts of gold.","created_at":"2020-07-22T09:07:45.614000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"735422827678793800","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
